# image 1
Style: Chinese Ink Wash (Sumi-e)
Aspect Ratio: 16:9
An artistic illustration for the tea page "Mengding Ganlu (Sweet Dew)": the five misty peaks of Meng Mountain in western Sichuan rising through low cloud at early morning, a small Tang-era temple roofline half hidden among pines on a ridge, terraced tea bushes descending the slope, and in the close foreground a scatter of tightly curled downy green tea threads beside a shallow porcelain cup of pale yellow-green liquor with dew beading on a leaf; wet-on-wet ink wash textures, restrained jade, silver and warm grey palette, soft paper grain; calm, minimal, museum-poster feel; no text, no letters, no characters, no logos.
